From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:16:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: Drop the calls of the interface the active context
 state does not emulate.

With a state emulating ID3D10Device active, Windows 11 drops what the
immediate context is asked to set, draw, dispatch, copy, update, clear
or generate, and what it is asked for is what an empty state has (only
PSGetSamplers leaves the samplers alone); maps, queries and flushes
still work.  It is the same the other way round for ID3D10Device with
a D3D11 state (tools/startupgapsprobe d3d10emu, d3d10emu2).  Wine ran
both, and printed that the emulation was not done; now it is, and the
D3D10 methods that called the D3D11 ones call their bodies instead.

A device made through D3D11CoreCreateDevice had its first state marked
as emulating ID3D10Device1, since it is made before the device is known
to be a D3D11 one; it is marked as a D3D11 state now.  The copies shared
surfaces make go round the check, as d3d11 makes them itself.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c b/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c
index 50b7d8edd38..852cf7879d1 100644
--- a/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d11/d3d11_main.c
@@ -139,6 +139,9 @@ HRESULT WINAPI D3D11CoreCreateDevice(IDXGIFactory *factory, IDXGIAdapter *adapte
     }
     d3d_device->d3d11_only = TRUE;
     d3d_device->create_flags = flags;
+    /* The first state was made with the device, before it was known to be a D3D11 one. */
+    if (d3d_device->state)
+        d3d_device->state->emulated_interface = IID_ID3D11Device5;
 
     return S_OK;
 }
